# Freeze the (interactively set) wall origin and bake it into the named plan.
# The origin is given in the world frame; only x and y and yaw are used for
# the wall pose. z is the ground reference for the bottom course, but this
# request's z is only a fallback: wall_setup_node queries the detector's
# local ground-plane fit (DiscoverBlocks.ground_height_m) and, if that
# succeeds, overwrites z with the measured value before freezing -- the z
# given here is used as-is only when that query is unavailable.
string wall_plan_name
geometry_msgs/Pose origin
bool persist          # if true, write the resolved per-block plan back to disk
---
bool success
bool valid            # all resolved blocks passed reach/collision validation
uint32 num_blocks
string message
